[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5396816522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122764#issuecomment-5396816522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122764","id":5396816522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQaziig","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T14:40:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:43:10Z","body":"One option for long term goal of having the symbols be served on-demand would be to have a choice in the crash handler to fetch the symbols using `debuginfod` if integrated directly (not sure what license would be required for that)\r\n\r\nBut if we don't integrate it directly we can still integrate the lookup for it, and then have the crash handler on Linux (at least for official editor and template builds) prompt the user to run `debuginfod-find` on the executable, with some clear instructions on how to do that etc., and then when running again it would be able to fetch the debug information from that\r\n\r\nIf we host the debug symbols in some debuginfod repository (not sure if there are official services for that, but we could host it ourselves relatively simply), then just running `debuginfod-find debuginfo {program}` will fetch the debug information automatically if it is available, assuming the executable has a proper `.note.gnu.build-id` generated and an associated entry exists on some database, it will then be available directly for both gdb and the crash handler assuming it goes into an appropriate location and we look at that location","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5396816522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5398802796","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122764#issuecomment-5398802796","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122764","id":5398802796,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQcsxbA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_ev